  <iati-identifier>NL-KVK-27363950-IMVO-TruStone</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-27363950" type="15">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sociaal-Economische Raad</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TruStone Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The TruStone Initiative is a multi-stakeholder initiative in which companies, contracting authorities, industry associations, trade unions, NGOs and the government join forces to adress risks to people and the environment in the natural stones supply chains. The process is facilitated by the Dutch Social and Economic Council. The overall goal of the Initiative is to learn from each other and to increase leverage aimed at making international supply chains more sustainable and thereby contributing to the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Companies joining the TruStone Initiative are expected to conduct due diligence in line with the OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises and the United Nations Guiding Principles for Business and Human Rights (UNGPs). The scope of the Initiative consist of companies that sell natural stone in the Dutch and Belgian markets. The Agreement covers the entire supply chain of natural stone. More information can be found on https://www.imvoconvenanten.nl/en/trustone. For the final evaluation report of 2020-2024 see: https://www.imvoconvenanten.nl/-/media/imvo/files/natuursteen/eindevaluatie-trustone-2020-2024.pdf</narrative>
  </description>
